# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Tea Factory Digital — admin console
#  Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and adjust.
#
#  Only PUBLIC values belong here. A Vite `VITE_*` variable is compiled into the
#  bundle and readable by anyone with the URL — it is configuration, never a
#  secret. No API keys, no signing secrets.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The API origin. `{tenant}` is substituted with the resolved tenant id, which
# is the escape hatch that lets one factory be moved to its own deployment later
# without a console release (white-label.md → Where the tenant comes from).
#
#   shared deployment:   https://api.teafactory.example/v1
#   per-tenant origin:   https://{tenant}.api.teafactory.example/v1
#
# THIS IS A PLACEHOLDER ORIGIN. The backend does not exist yet; every path the
# console calls is specified in docs/api-contract.md. Point this at the real
# staging origin once it does.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.teafactory.example/v1

# Serve every request from the in-browser mock instead of the network.
#   1 → MSW intercepts, seeded from src/services/mocks/seed.ts
#   0 → real HTTP to VITE_API_BASE_URL
# Default while the backend is unbuilt: 1.
VITE_USE_MOCK=1

# Tenant used when the host carries no subdomain (i.e. localhost).
# In production the subdomain answers this and the value is ignored.
VITE_DEFAULT_TENANT=galaboda

# Also send `X-Tenant` alongside the subdomain. The backend must treat it as a
# ROUTING HINT ONLY and validate it against the token — a header that disagrees
# with the token is a 403, never a tenant switch.
VITE_SEND_TENANT_HEADER=1

# Double-submit CSRF. The API sets a NON-httpOnly cookie; the console echoes its
# value back in a header on every mutation, including the token refresh.
#
# Not what makes refresh work — the console and the API share a site
# (*.teafactory.lk), so the SameSite=Lax refresh cookie is sent across the
# subdomain split regardless. This defends the case Lax cannot: a compromised
# SIBLING subdomain, which is same-site and could otherwise drive a refresh.
#
# Leave VITE_CSRF_COOKIE empty to switch it off for an API that issues no cookie.
VITE_CSRF_COOKIE=tfd_csrf
VITE_CSRF_HEADER=X-CSRF-Token

# Request timeout, ms. Do not shorten for a rural network: the API and the
# office share a connection with the phones (§20.1).
VITE_API_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
